p.src:
For example, with the convention $R^\rho{}_{\sigma\mu\nu}
=\partial_\mu\Gamma^\rho_{\nu\sigma}
-\partial_\nu\Gamma^\rho_{\mu\sigma}+\cdots,$ the lowered tensor at $P$ is a linear combination of second metric derivatives, $R_{\alpha\beta\gamma\delta}(P)
  =
  \frac12\left(
  g_{\alpha\delta,\beta\gamma}
  g_{\beta\gamma,\alpha\delta}
  -g_{\alpha\gamma,\beta\delta}
  -g_{\beta\delta,\alpha\gamma}
  \right)_P.$

